    "text": [
  "<h1>8 Types of Developers</h1>",
  "<p>In this post we are going to take a look at some typical personality traits of developers. And based on their characteristics I have made some broad classifications of developers.</p>",
  "<p>I am not sure these classifications are truly meaningful or really exist in the workplace, it's just a curious exploration and answer to the question 'What if these type of Developers exist in the real world and what would be their typical behaviors and what would be their preferences?'</p>",
  "<h1>1. The Altruist Developer</h1>",
  "<p>The Altruist developer is the one who cares about others. They are the ones who generally contribute to open source and create many open source packages. They write good documentation and are generally responsible for a lot of internal tooling within teams and organizations.</p>",
  "<img src='https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fj6swy9fzzdx0x95jd073.jpg' alt='The Altruist Developer' />",
  "<hr></hr>",
  "<h1>2. The Ambidextrous Developer</h1>",
  "<p>They could potentially be a FullStack Developer or a DevOps Engineer or an SRE. They are the go-getters in their teams. You can typically find these types of folks in early-stage startups or very small organizations.</p>",
  "<img src='https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fv9zucbfydvqe3fyqten2.jpg' alt='The Ambidextrous Developer' />",
  "<hr></hr>",
  "<h1>3. The Ascetic Developer</h1>",
  "<p>Minimalism is the motto for these developers. They have the typical characteristics of self-denial, austerity, and lonely contemplation.</p>",
  "<img src='https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqcbfhv65vdzssznzsxk3.jpg' alt='The Ascetic Developer' />",
  "<hr></hr>",
  "<h1>4. The Ego Maniac Developer</h1>",
  "<p>The first and foremost question these types of developers have in their mind is 'What's in it for me?'. Their selfishness, greed, and ruthless desire for self-advancement might hurt other people in the team.</p>",
  "<img src='https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ffhajlz7rn40nqun5g44f.jpg' alt='The Ego Maniac Developer' />",
  "<hr></hr>",
  "<h1>5. The Egotist Developer</h1>",
  "<p>These developers are obnoxious and typically carry narcissistic tendencies. They coerce their peers to approve their pull requests and love showing off their intellectual prowess.</p>",
  "<img src='https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F6nwi35546v6h8s4ydmfd.jpg' alt='The Egotist Developer' />",
  "<hr></hr>",
  "<h1>6. The Extrovert Developer</h1>",
  "<p>These developers love meetings and social interaction. They dread quiet offices and thrive in environments with high collaboration.</p>",
  "<img src='https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fc6hk2lkd3tfh6umrc54t.jpg' alt='The Extrovert Developer' />",
  "<hr></hr>",
  "<h1>7. The Introvert Developer</h1>",
  "<p>They are the opposite of extroverts. They prefer working alone, avoid meetings, and hate pair programming.</p>",
  "<img src='https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqkd2t4p0iqfuzmkole7o.jpg' alt='The Introvert Developer' />",
  "<h1>8. The Misanthropic Developer</h1>",
  "<p>They distrust humans, prefer automation, and rely on machines more than people. They are big fans of shell scripting and prefer working independently.</p>",
  "<img src='https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F07g577140qu3omjy3zq7.jpg' alt='The Misanthropic Developer' />"
],
